 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? It depends how hot it is. In general, every twenty minutes or so, stopping and filling up from a water bottle that's sitting on handlebars. Then small bottles with few mouths between riders help. A typical ride might need a quart to two liters, depending on the weather. A bar here and there is fine, but full energy bars can make you feel gross. A small bag of dry snacks is much nicer. You can, but it's much faster to start with full tank. And if you do run short, cafes are usually only a few minutes away.",
